<p><strong>Boys, Beasts & Men</strong> by Sam J. Miller; <strong>Missoula</strong> by Jon Krakauer; <strong>City of Stairs</strong> by Robert Jackson Bennett; <strong>Angels Before Man</strong> by Rafael Nicolás; <strong>The Old Man and the Sea</strong> by Ernest Hemingway; <strong>Dune</strong> by Frank Herbert; <strong>The Hitchhikers Guide to the Galaxy</strong> by Douglas Adams; <strong>Of Mice and Men</strong> by John Steinbeck; <strong>Animal Farm</strong> by George Orwell; <strong>To Kill a Mockingbird</strong> by Harper Lee; <strong>Girl, Interrupted</strong> by Susanna Kaysen; <strong>Fight Club</strong> by Chuck Palahniuk; <strong>Monsters of Men</strong> by Patrick Ness; <strong>The Ask and the Answer</strong> by Patrick Ness; <strong>The Knife of Never Letting Go</strong> by Patrick Ness; <strong>Neuromancer</strong> by William Gibson; <strong>1984</strong> by George Orwell; and many more I am probably forgetting!</p>
			
<h2>Anime I've watched</h2>
